        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Most residential roof replacements in Utah take one to three days for standard asphalt shingle homes. Larger homes, steep slopes, or complex materials like tile and metal can extend the project timeline to three to five days.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "one to three days for standard asphalt shingle homes"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Factors That Affect the Timeline"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Size and Pitch: Larger square footage and steep, multi-facet angles slow down tear-off and installation.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Material Type: Standard asphalt shingles take 1 to 2 days, while heavy concrete/clay tiles or standing-seam metal systems often require 3 to 5 days or more.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hidden Decking Damage: Finding rotten or water-damaged plywood underneath old shingles during the tear-off phase adds repair time."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Utah Weather: Sudden mountain storms, high winds, or heavy winter snow can pause work, though professional crews seal and protect your home overnight to prevent exposure."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to share, what are the approximate square footage, current material (shingle, metal, tile), and pitch/steepness of your roof? I can give you a more customized time estimate."
      }
